Construct the route $O\to X\to C$, first parallel to $\mathbf{b}$ and then parallel to $\mathbf{a}$.

Along $OX$, move $2$ squares right and $2$ squares down. A copy of $\mathbf{b}$ moves $1$ square left and $1$ square up. Thus $OX=2|\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the opposite direction to $\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\overrightarrow{OX}=-2\mathbf{b}$.

