Construct the route $O\to X\to C$, first parallel to $\mathbf{b}$ and then parallel to $\mathbf{a}$.

Along $OX$, move $2$ squares right and $2$ squares down. A copy of $\mathbf{b}$ moves $1$ square left and $1$ square up. Thus $OX=2|\mathbf{b}|$ and the segment points in the opposite direction to $\mathbf{b}$. Hence $\overrightarrow{OX}=-2\mathbf{b}$.

Along $XC$, move $1$ square left. A copy of $\mathbf{a}$ moves $2$ squares left. Thus $XC=\frac{1}{2}|\mathbf{a}|$ and the segment points in the same direction to $\mathbf{a}$. Hence $\overrightarrow{XC}=\frac{1}{2}\mathbf{a}$.

$$
\begin{aligned}
\mathbf{c}&=\overrightarrow{OX}+\overrightarrow{XC}\\&=-2\mathbf{b}+\frac{1}{2}\mathbf{a}\\&=\frac{1}{2}\mathbf{a}-2\mathbf{b}
\end{aligned}
$$

